---
layout: layouts/base.njk
title: "Emergency Support | Pikes Peak Web Designs"
description: "For existing clients: site down, dangerous error, or anything costing you business right now. Emergencies skip the queue, and I am available for quick turnarounds on most business days."
noindex: true
---

<section class="page-hero">
  <div class="container">
    <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/">Home</a><span class="sep">/</span><a href="/client-portal/">Client Portal</a><span class="sep">/</span><span>Emergency Support</span>
    </nav>
    <span class="section-label">Urgent issues</span>
    <h1>Something's wrong. <em>We fix it fast.</em></h1>
    <p>Use this form if your site is down, displaying wrong information that is costing you business, or has a security concern. Emergencies skip the queue and get handled fast on most business days.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="container" style="max-width:720px">
    <div class="form-callout form-callout--danger">
      <strong>Call us if it's truly urgent.</strong>
      <span>Text or call <a href="tel:{{ site.phone }}" class="inline-link">{{ site.phoneDisplay }}</a> for immediate attention. The form is a backup and a way to put all the detail in one place, but phone is faster when the clock matters.</span>
    </div>

    <div class="contact-form-card">
      <h2 class="form-heading">Describe the emergency</h2>
      <p class="form-intro">Give us as much detail as you can. Screenshots help. I will start investigating the moment the form lands.</p>

      <form data-web3forms data-redirect="/thank-you/?type=emergency" action="https://api.web3forms.com/submit" method="POST" class="form">
        <input type="hidden" name="access_key" value="b6c3454b-f07c-43f7-9070-0e0cb5286f55">
        <input type="hidden" name="subject" value="[EMERGENCY] Pikes Peak Web Designs client">
        <input type="hidden" name="from_name" value="Pikes Peak Emergency">
        <input type="checkbox" name="botcheck" style="display:none" tabindex="-1" autocomplete="off">

        <div class="form-row">
          <div class="form-group">
            <label for="businessName">Business name <span class="req">*</span></label>
            <input type="text" id="businessName" name="businessName" required autocomplete="organization">
          </div>
          <div class="form-group">
            <label for="phone">Best phone to reach you <span class="req">*</span></label>
            <input type="tel" id="phone" name="phone" required autocomplete="tel">
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="form-group">
          <label for="email">Email <span class="req">*</span></label>
          <input type="email" id="email" name="email" required autocomplete="email">
        </div>

        <div class="form-group">
          <label for="severity">How bad is it right now? <span class="req">*</span></label>
          <select id="severity" name="severity" required>
            <option value="">Choose one…</option>
            <option value="site-down">Site is completely down</option>
            <option value="partial-outage">Part of the site is broken (form, page, checkout, etc.)</option>
            <option value="wrong-info">Wrong information is live and costing us business</option>
            <option value="security">Security concern (suspicious activity, defaced content)</option>
            <option value="other-urgent">Other urgent issue; I'll explain below</option>
          </select>
        </div>

        <div class="form-group">
          <label for="whenStarted">When did the issue start?</label>
          <input type="text" id="whenStarted" name="whenStarted" placeholder="e.g. 'About 2 hours ago' or 'Since this morning'">
        </div>

        <div class="form-group">
          <label for="affectedUrl">Which URL or page is affected?</label>
          <input type="text" id="affectedUrl" name="affectedUrl" placeholder="e.g. yourbusiness.com/contact/">
        </div>

        <div class="form-group">
          <label for="description">What's happening? <span class="req">*</span></label>
          <textarea id="description" name="description" rows="6" placeholder="Describe what you or your customers are seeing. Include any error messages. If you have a screenshot, paste a link to it." required></textarea>
        </div>

        <div class="form-group">
          <label for="screenshotLink">Screenshot link (if you have one)</label>
          <input type="url" id="screenshotLink" name="screenshotLink" placeholder="https://">
        </div>

        <div id="form-error" role="alert" class="form-error">
          Something went wrong submitting this. Please call <a href="tel:{{ site.phone }}">{{ site.phoneDisplay }}</a> immediately.
        </div>

        <button type="submit" class="btn btn-primary btn-full btn-lg">Submit emergency request</button>
        <p class="form-hint">If this is truly time-critical, <strong>call me</strong> at <a href="tel:{{ site.phone }}" class="inline-link">{{ site.phoneDisplay }}</a>; I pick up or call back quickly.</p>
      </form>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
